{Here Black lost on time. "the position that will be engraved on Sugden's
heart. Black should play what he intended, namely} 44... a3 {and if} 45. Qxa3 (
{or if} 45. e5 a2 {as his queen guards against mate on e8.}) 45... Qe2+ {
etc. Black's explanation was that he thought he still had a minute left. The
spectators showed amazing discipline, although their hands must have been
itching like mine to make the winning move!" (Cafferty) Source: BCM, May 1969,
p145} 1-0

